        "original_id": "5b5c5f83-e4e8-5d7e-b408-b25e92660e47",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Randy Savage, Lanny Poffo, The Great Muta\n- Organizations: World Wrestling Federation (WWF/WWE), World Championship Wrestling (WCW)\n- Places: Atlanta, Georgia, Japan, North America\n- Roles: professional wrestler, color commentator\n- Concepts: ring names, moonsault\n\nFacts:\n- Randy Savage was born as Randy Mario Poffo on November 15, 1952, and he died on May 20, 2011.\n- Randy Savage was an American professional wrestler and color commentator who was better known by the ring name \"Macho Man\" Randy Savage.\n- Randy Savage was best known for his time in the World Wrestling Federation, now called WWE, and later in World Championship Wrestling.\n- World Championship Wrestling, Inc. was an American professional wrestling promotion based in Atlanta, Georgia.\n- Lanny Poffo was the real-life younger brother of Randy Savage.\n- The moonsault gained much of its popularity in Japanese and American wrestling through The Great Muta.\n- Lanny Poffo used the moonsault in North America years before The Great Muta arrived from Japan.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
